&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Relationship Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department / Function:&lt;/strong&gt; Commercial &amp;amp; Field Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports To:&lt;/strong&gt; State Coordinator&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Field-based, Nigeria&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive base salary + performance-based commission&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Moniepoint&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month. As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions and process over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drives business growth by expanding our merchant footprint, building high-value customer relationships, and introducing financial solutions tailored to local business needs. This role is responsible for end-to-end merchant acquisition, terminal deployment, and account retention across assigned commercial areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Identify, visit, and onboard prospective merchants through field engagement, referrals, and local trade community outreach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Educate business owners on Moniepoint’s suite of products, recommending solutions that match their operational and growth goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Achieve and exceed monthly targets for active merchant onboarding, terminal deployment, loan disbursements, and repayments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Oversee end-to-end merchant onboarding, ensuring accurate KYC documentation and strict adherence to operational SOPs and regulatory guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Build and nurture long-term relationships with merchants to encourage account activity, high transaction volume, and ongoing retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Conduct transparent discussions on pricing, terms, and agreements within established company guidelines to build trusted partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Serve as the primary point of contact for customer queries, resolving issues promptly or escalating complex operational needs appropriately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Gather local market intelligence and competitor activity, providing actionable feedback to field leadership to help refine growth tactics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Maintain accurate pipeline records and submit timely field performance reports using CRM tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Bachelor’s degree, Higher National Diploma (HND), or Ordinary National Diploma (OND) from a recognised tertiary institution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ 2 to 4 years of hands-on sales experience, preferably within banking, fintech, payment services, or fast-moving commercial environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Proven track record of meeting or exceeding targets in merchant onboarding, field sales, or client acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Deep understanding of the local financial services landscape and regional trading dynamics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Strong communication and customer relationship skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Practical experience with POS terminal deployment, payment acquiring, or business loan products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;→ Proficiency in CRM software for field tracking, pipeline management, and activity reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Culture -We put our people first and prioritize the well-being of every team member. We’ve built a company where all opinions carry weight and where all voices are heard. We value and respect each other and always look out for one another. Above all, we are human.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Learning - We have a learning and development-focused environment with an emphasis on knowledge sharing, training, and regular internal technical talks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Compensation - You’ll receive an attractive salary, pension, health insurance, annual bonus, plus other benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect in the hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A preliminary phone call with the recruiter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An interview with the Hiring Team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An interview with a member of our Executive team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
